IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pl-types`

-- Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 — GOAL 1: ELIGIBILITY.
--
--   "Is this version of the Act the one that applies to the child; is the
--    person the primary carer; which employment test do they meet; do they
--    meet the parental leave payment threshold test; and does s 4 or s 6
--    keep them from leave under this Act?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1987_129.txt — ss 2, 2B,
-- 2BA, 4, 6, 7, 72A, 76; Schedule 1AA.

§ `Goal 1 — eligibility`

§§ `Days and dates`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The date the Act measures from, throughout: "the expected date of delivery
-- of the child (in the case of a child to be born to the employee or to the
-- employee's spouse or partner); or the first date on which either the
-- employee or the employee's spouse or partner becomes the primary carer in
-- respect of the child (in any other case)" (ss 2, 2BA(4), 55, 56, 71CAA).
@ref ss 2, 2BA, 71CAA
GIVEN c IS A Child
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the tests look back from, for` c MEANS
    IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
    THEN c's `expected date of delivery`
    ELSE c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer`

-- FORK F4: ss 6 and 71F are measured to the day the leave or the payments
-- start, taken as the date of birth (or, before the birth, the expected date
-- of delivery) for a child born to the person or their spouse or partner,
-- and the date of becoming the primary carer otherwise (ss 10, 71K).
@ref ss 6, 10, 71F, 71K
GIVEN c IS A Child
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the leave or payments start, for` c MEANS
    IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
    THEN CONSIDER c's `date of birth`
         WHEN JUST b THEN b
         WHEN NOTHING THEN c's `expected date of delivery`
    ELSE c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer`

§§ `Which version applies (Schedule 1AA cl 5)`

-- Schedule 1AA cl 5(1): "This Act, as amended by Part 2 of the Parental Leave
-- and Employment Protection Amendment Act 2017, applies to a person who takes
-- parental leave or applies for a parental leave payment in respect of a
-- child if,— (a) in the case of a child born to the person or to the person's
-- spouse or partner,— (i) the expected date of delivery of the child is on or
-- after 1 July 2020; or (ii) the child is born on or after 1 July 2020; or
-- (b) in any other case, the person or his or her spouse or partner becomes
-- the primary carer in respect of a child on or after 1 July 2020." Earlier
-- children fall under the Act as it stood before (22 weeks, and earlier
-- figures), which the text does not carry.
@ref Schedule 1AA cl 5
GIVEN c IS A Child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this version applies to` c IF
    IF   c's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
    THEN     c's `expected date of delivery` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2020
         OR  CONSIDER c's `date of birth`
             WHEN JUST b THEN b AT LEAST Date 1 7 2020
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    ELSE c's `first date the person or their spouse or partner becomes the primary carer` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2020

§§ `The primary carer (s 7)`

-- s 7(1) "primary carer means— (a) a female (the biological mother) who is
-- pregnant or has given birth to a child: (b) the spouse or partner of the
-- biological mother, only if— (i) the spouse or partner has succeeded under
-- section 72B ...; or (ii) the biological mother has transferred all or part
-- of her entitlement to a parental leave payment to that spouse or partner
-- under section 71E ...; or (iii) neither subparagraph (i) nor (ii) applies
-- and all of the following are true: (A) the child is under 1 year of age;
-- and (B) the spouse or partner ... has taken permanent primary
-- responsibility ... to the exclusion of the biological mother; and (C) ...
-- the biological mother either had not applied for, or did not qualify to
-- apply for, a parental leave payment: (c) a person, other than the
-- biological mother or her spouse or partner, who takes permanent primary
-- responsibility ... of a child who is under the age of 6 years (and if there
-- is more than 1 such person, the person nominated in accordance with
-- subsection (2))." (2) applies only "If 2 or more persons meet the
-- criterion in subsection (1)(c)"; a sole carer needs no nomination.
@ref s 7
@export Who is the primary carer under s 7 of the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ): the biological mother; her spouse or partner if they succeeded to her entitlement (s 72B), received a transfer (s 71E), or took permanent primary responsibility for a child under 1 to her exclusion when she had not applied or did not qualify; or another person who took permanent primary responsibility for a child under 6 (the one nominated, if several). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Carer facts`  @desc Whether the person is the biological mother or her spouse or partner, whether they succeeded or received a transfer, whether they took permanent primary responsibility and the child's age in months then, whether the mother had applied and qualified for a payment, and whether they are the nominated person
GIVETH A `Primary carer kind`
`the primary carer kind of` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF f's `is the biological mother` THEN `(a) the biological mother`
        IF f's `is the biological mother's spouse or partner` AND f's `has succeeded under s 72B`
            THEN `(b)(i) the mother's spouse or partner who has succeeded under s 72B`
        IF f's `is the biological mother's spouse or partner` AND f's `has received a transfer under s 71E`
            THEN `(b)(ii) the mother's spouse or partner to whom she transferred under s 71E`
        IF     f's `is the biological mother's spouse or partner`
           AND f's `has taken permanent primary responsibility`
           AND f's `age of the child in months when that responsibility was taken` LESS THAN 12
           AND NOT f's `the mother had applied, and qualified, for a payment then`
            THEN `(b)(iii) the mother's spouse or partner who took permanent primary responsibility`
        IF     NOT f's `is the biological mother's spouse or partner`
           AND f's `has taken permanent primary responsibility`
           AND f's `age of the child in months when that responsibility was taken` LESS THAN 72
           AND ((NOT f's `another person also meets s 7(1)(c)`) OR f's `is the person nominated under s 7(2)`)
            THEN `(c) another person who took permanent primary responsibility`
        OTHERWISE `not the primary carer`

GIVEN f IS A `Carer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the primary carer` f IF
    NOT `the primary carer kind of` f EQUALS `not the primary carer`

§§ `The employment tests (s 2BA(1))`

-- s 2BA(1) "(a) an employee meets the 6-month employment test if the
-- employee will have been employed by the same employer for at least an
-- average of 10 hours a week in the 6 months immediately preceding the
-- expected date of— (i) delivery of the child ...; or (ii) assumption of
-- responsibility for the care of the child ...: (b) an employee meets the
-- 12-month employment test if ... in the 12 months immediately preceding".
-- The 12-month test is reported where both are met.
@ref s 2BA(1), (3)
@export Which employment test an employee meets under s 2BA(1) of the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ): the 12-month test if employed by the same employer for the 12 months before the expected date of delivery (or of assuming care) at an average of at least 10 hours a week; otherwise the 6-month test on the same terms over 6 months; otherwise neither. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment with the employer`  @desc When the employment with the same employer began, and the average weekly hours over the 6 and 12 months before the date (after s 72A)
      from IS A DATE  @desc The expected date of delivery, or of assuming responsibility for the care of the child
GIVETH AN `Employment test`
`the employment test met by` e `before` from MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     e's `employed by the same employer since` AT MOST `add months` from (0 MINUS 12)
           AND e's `average weekly hours over the 12 months` AT LEAST 10
            THEN `the 12-month employment test`
        IF     e's `employed by the same employer since` AT MOST `add months` from (0 MINUS 6)
           AND e's `average weekly hours over the 6 months` AT LEAST 10
            THEN `the 6-month employment test`
        OTHERWISE `neither employment test`

GIVEN t IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets an employment test` t IF
    NOT t EQUALS `neither employment test`

§§ `The parental leave payment threshold test (s 2BA(4))`

-- s 2BA(4) "(a) an employee meets the parental leave payment threshold test
-- if he or she will have been employed as an employee for at least an
-- average of 10 hours a week for any 26 of the 52 weeks immediately
-- preceding" the date; "(b) a self-employed person ... self-employed for at
-- least an average of 10 hours a week for any 26 of the 52 weeks". FORK F7:
-- the person must have been employed (or self-employed) in at least 26 of
-- the 52 weeks, and some 26 of those weeks must average 10 hours. A week
-- with no hours (after s 72A or s 71CB(2)) is a week not employed. The 26
-- weeks averaging 10 hours exist exactly when the 26 busiest weeks total at
-- least 260 hours.
@ref s 2BA(4)
GIVEN weekly IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of the 26 highest of` weekly MEANS
    sum (take 26 (reverse (sort weekly)))

@ref s 2BA(4)
GIVEN hours IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `averages 10 hours a week over some 26 of the 52 weeks` hours IF
        count (filter (GIVEN h YIELD h GREATER THAN 0) hours) AT LEAST 26
    AND `the total of the 26 highest of` hours AT LEAST 260

@ref s 2BA(4), s 2AD
@export Whether a person meets the parental leave payment threshold test under s 2BA(4) of the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ): an average of at least 10 hours a week, as an employee or as a self-employed person (each counted separately, s 2AD), over any 26 of the 52 weeks before the expected date of delivery or of becoming the primary carer. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`  @desc The hours worked as an employee and as a self-employed person in each of the 52 weeks
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the parental leave payment threshold test` p IF
        (p's `an employee for the payment` AND `averages 10 hours a week over some 26 of the 52 weeks` (p's `hours as an employee in each of the 52 weeks`))
    OR  (p's `self-employed for the payment` AND `averages 10 hours a week over some 26 of the 52 weeks` (p's `hours self-employed in each of the 52 weeks`))

§§ `Restrictions (ss 4, 6)`

-- s 4(1) "Parts 1 to 5 apply to all employees except employees who have
-- rights and benefits in the nature of parental leave that are,— (a) in
-- their overall effect, as favourable ... or more favourable ...; and (b)
-- provided under a comprehensive employment agreement or other
-- arrangement". (2) comprehensive "if it effectively addresses all of" five
-- matters.
@ref s 4
GIVEN `as favourable` IS A BOOLEAN, `matters addressed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 1 to 5 apply, other arrangement as favourable:` `as favourable` `, s 4(2) matters it addresses` `matters addressed` IF
    NOT (`as favourable` AND `matters addressed` AT LEAST 5)

-- s 6 "An employee shall not be entitled to parental leave in respect of a
-- child by virtue of this Act if— (a) that employee has previously taken,
-- in respect of another child, a period of leave ...; and (b) less than 6
-- months have elapsed since the day after the date on which the most recent
-- period of leave referred to in paragraph (a) ended."
@ref s 6
GIVEN previous IS A MAYBE DATE, start IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 bars leave, previous leave for another child ended` previous `, leave starting` start IF
    CONSIDER previous
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST ended THEN start LESS THAN `add months` (`the day` 1 `days after` ended) 6
